              "width": 597,
              "height": 332
            }
          ],
          "gen": true
        },
        {
          "type": "text",
          "html": "Driller is a pneumatic drilling unit for the holes the diamond wire passes through. With a pneumatic rotary head and a down-the-hole (DTH) hammer it reaches depths of 25 - 30 metres even in rock with natural irregularities, at a high drilling speed.",
          "gen": true
        },
        {
          "type": "text",
          "html": "Light and versatile structure for drilling in any direction and flush with the quarry floor. Column for extension rods of 1,000 or 1,500 mm, a down-the-hole hammer up to 3 inches for holes up to 95 mm, and a down jack with a ball joint for drilling in any direction. The pneumatic control panel with centralised lubrication can be turned in any direction. Feed by a piston motor (8.5 kN) or a vane motor (4.8 kN). A hydraulic version is available as Driller ID.",
          "gen": true
        },
        {
          "type": "heading",
          "level": 3,
          "text": "Two versions",
          "gen": true
        },
        {
          "type": "text",
          "html": "ID in the model name stands for the hydraulic version.",
          "gen": true
        },
        {
          "type": "list",
          "ordered": false,
          "items": [
            "Pneumatic (Driller): feed stroke 1,000 - 1,500 mm, rotary torque 850 Nm, air consumption 8 m³/min, weight 180 kg",
            "Hydraulic (Driller ID): feed stroke 1,760 mm, rotary torque 1,600 Nm, rotary speed 35 - 100 rpm, weight 145 kg"
          ],
          "gen": true
        },
